  ],
  "steps": [
    "Resolve configurable combinations of classname/name/file/external_id; keep same names with different selected Class/File contexts distinct, never infer an identifier from unknown XML or target metadata.",
    "Account for every testcase occurrence and return separate unmapped, ambiguous and contradictory diagnostics with grouped occurrence/mapping indices; retain only independently unambiguous candidates without choosing an import policy.",
    "Reject foreign source hashes, out-of-range or duplicate sidecar ordinals, unsafe types, invalid schemas and exceeded hard input boundaries without external access or partial publication.",
    "Preserve strict W behavior, native outcome classes, owned raw/canonical provenance, complete coverage of rejected occurrences, linear grouped diagnostics and isolated Core/PYZ behavior.",
    "12.i.R additionally binds exact Generic/SARIF originals and applies explicit abort/skip to record-local required-field, binding and mapping failures. Every source occurrence is accepted, rejected with diagnostics or withheld by abort; conflicting or ambiguous observations cannot select a favorable result. Global envelope/source/target/resource errors remain fatal; no persistence or external authority is granted."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "Nicht gemappte, mehrdeutig gemappte oder widersprüchliche Testergebnisse MÜSSEN als getrennte Diagnosen erscheinen.",
    "scope": "12.g.R provides complete separate unmapped, ambiguous and contradictory JUnit mapping observations, grouped by exact selected identity and full Class/Name/File/External-ID context, with every rejected occurrence accounted for. Diagnostic groups are linear rather than pairwise. The passive diagnostics do not publish Evidence or authorize an external run. 12.i.R additionally binds exact Generic/SARIF originals and applies explicit abort/skip to record-local required-field, binding and mapping failures. Every source occurrence is accepted, rejected with diagnostics or withheld by abort; conflicting or ambiguous observations cannot select a favorable result. Global envelope/source/target/resource errors remain fatal; no persistence or external authority is granted."
